### ───────────── Notes ─────────────
# The same requests run against both backends. To switch, comment out one @host
# line and leave the other active:
#   3000 = NestJS  (apps/api,        npm run start:dev -w api)
#   5000 = .NET    (apps/api-dotnet, dotnet run)
#
# Not built on both sides yet: PATCH exists in NestJS only (issue #3). On port
# 5000 the route answers 405 until then — it knows GET and DELETE only.
#
# The status code is the contract, the error body is not: Nest sends
# { statusCode, message, error }, ASP.NET Core sends RFC 9457 ProblemDetails.
# A deliberate difference, see docs/DECISIONS.md.
#
# Three requests are named (# @name …). Later requests reach into their response
# with {{name.response.body.$.id}}, so no UUID has to be pasted by hand. This
# needs the named request to have been sent once in this editor session. If the
# variable stays unresolved, paste the id from the response instead.
#
# The starting point is the seed (npx prisma db seed from apps/api): the recipes
# Langos and Römertopfbrot, 17 ingredients.

# @host = http://localhost:3000
@host = http://localhost:5000


### ───────────── GET /recipes ─────────────

### All recipes, ordered by title -> 200
### Named: the detail requests below take their id from this response.
# @name recipeList
GET {{host}}/recipes

### Prefix of a word: finds Langos -> 200
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=lang

### Case does not matter: finds Langos -> 200 (ILIKE on recipe.title)
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=LANGOS

### Substring in the middle: finds Römertopfbrot -> 200
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=brot

### Umlaut as written: finds Römertopfbrot -> 200
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=römer

### Umlaut transliterated: finds nothing -> 200 with []
### Titles have no normalized column, "oe" is not resolved.
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=roemer

### Search without a hit -> 200 with []
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=xyz

### Empty search term: no filter, every recipe -> 200
GET {{host}}/recipes?search=


### ───────────── GET /recipes/:id ─────────────

### First recipe from the list, including its ingredients -> 200
### Ingredients ordered by position, groupLabel and note per line.
GET {{host}}/recipes/{{recipeList.response.body.$[0].id}}

### Unknown but valid UUID v7 -> 404
GET {{host}}/recipes/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### Valid UUID v4 -> 400 in Nest, 404 in .NET
### A deliberate difference: ParseUUIDPipe checks the version, Guid has no notion
### of one.
GET {{host}}/recipes/3f6b2c1e-8a4d-4f7b-9c2e-5d1a7b3f8e60

### Not a UUID -> 400
GET {{host}}/recipes/hallo


### ───────────── POST /recipes ─────────────

### Create a recipe -> 201
### Six ingredient lines, but five ingredients: "Salz" and "  SALZ  " normalize
### to the same ingredient row and differ only in note and position. Sending it
### twice changes nothing about that — the ingredients are reused, only the
### recipe is new.
### Named: the PATCH section below works on this recipe.
# @name newRecipe
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "description": "Reicht für zwei große Teller.",
  "servings": 2,
  "prepMinutes": 20,
  "totalMinutes": 45,
  "instructions": "1. Kartoffeln und Möhren **grob** würfeln.\n2. In der Brühe 20 Min. kochen, dann grob pürieren.\n3. Mit Salz und Majoran abschmecken.\n\n- schmeckt am zweiten Tag besser\n- Würstchen passen dazu",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM", "groupLabel": "Für die Suppe" },
    { "name": "Möhren", "amount": 2, "unit": "PIECE", "note": "mittelgroß", "groupLabel": "Für die Suppe" },
    { "name": "Gemüsebrühe", "amount": 1, "unit": "LITER", "groupLabel": "Für die Suppe" },
    { "name": "Salz", "amount": 1, "unit": "TEASPOON", "groupLabel": "Für die Suppe" },
    { "name": "  SALZ  ", "note": "zum Abschmecken", "groupLabel": "Zum Abschmecken" },
    { "name": "Majoran", "note": "getrocknet", "groupLabel": "Zum Abschmecken" }
  ]
}

### Required fields only -> 201 with servings 2
### The default comes from the database, not from the DTO. The second ingredient
### line has neither amount nor unit — "salt to taste" is a valid case.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spiegelei",
  "instructions": "Butter in der Pfanne schmelzen, Ei hineingleiten lassen, salzen.",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Ei", "amount": 2, "unit": "PIECE" },
    { "name": "Salz" }
  ]
}

### servings given -> 201 with servings 4
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe für vier",
  "instructions": "Wie oben, alles verdoppelt.",
  "servings": 4,
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 1600, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### Title of spaces only -> 400 (trimmed before it is validated)
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "   ",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### Empty ingredient list -> 400
### A recipe without ingredients is a text file.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": []
}

### Ingredient line without a name -> 400 (the message names ingredients[0].name)
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": [
    { "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### Unknown field sourceUrl -> 400
### sourceUrl, sourceName and externalId are columns in the table but not in the
### DTO — they belong to the V3 importer.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "sourceUrl": "https://example.org/kartoffelsuppe",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### Unit outside the enum -> 400 (the message names ingredients[0].unit)
### "EL" is the display form, TABLESPOON is what gets stored.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Mehl", "amount": 1, "unit": "EL" }
  ]
}

### servings null -> 400
### The field may be omitted but must not be null: null would violate the
### NOT NULL column and end as a 500.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "servings": null,
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### prepMinutes 0 -> 400 (times are positive or absent altogether)
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "prepMinutes": 0,
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" }
  ]
}

### amount with three decimal places -> 400
### numeric(8,2) would silently round it to 1.50.
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Mehl", "amount": 1.505, "unit": "TABLESPOON" }
  ]
}

### amount 0 -> 400 (amounts are positive; no amount means leaving it out)
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Kartoffelsuppe",
  "instructions": "Kartoffeln schälen …",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Mehl", "amount": 0, "unit": "TABLESPOON" }
  ]
}


### ───────────── PATCH /recipes/:id ─────────────
### NestJS only (issue #3). Works on the recipe from "Create a recipe" — send
### that POST once first.

### Change the title only -> 200
### A missing ingredients leaves the list untouched.
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Kartoffelcremesuppe" }

### Clear description with null -> 200, description is null afterwards
### Clearable fields may be null, required ones may not.
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "description": null }

### Replace the ingredient list only -> 200
### Four lines instead of six, positions 1–4, Pfeffer is new, Majoran is gone.
### The old lines are deleted rather than reconciled, so they come back with new
### ids. Check here: does updated_at change? Until the trigger migration (issue
### #9) the service sets the column itself, because a PATCH without recipe fields
### sends no UPDATE on recipe.
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Kartoffeln", "amount": 800, "unit": "GRAM" },
    { "name": "Möhren", "amount": 3, "unit": "PIECE" },
    { "name": "Gemüsebrühe", "amount": 1, "unit": "LITER" },
    { "name": "Pfeffer", "amount": 1, "unit": "PINCH", "note": "frisch gemahlen" }
  ]
}

### title null -> 400 (required, not clearable)
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": null }

### servings null -> 400
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "servings": null }

### Empty ingredient list -> 400 (rule inherited from the create DTO)
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/{{newRecipe.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ingredients": [] }

### Unknown but valid UUID -> 404
### Check afterwards: "Testpfeffer" must not be in ingredient. The recipe is
### looked up first, the ingredients are resolved only after that.
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Gibt es nicht",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Testpfeffer", "amount": 1, "unit": "PINCH" }
  ]
}

### Not a UUID -> 400
PATCH {{host}}/recipes/hallo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Kartoffelcremesuppe" }


### ───────────── DELETE /recipes/:id ─────────────

### Create a throwaway recipe to delete -> 201
# @name throwawayRecipe
POST {{host}}/recipes
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Zum Löschen",
  "instructions": "Wird gleich wieder gelöscht.",
  "ingredients": [
    { "name": "Testzutat", "amount": 1, "unit": "PIECE" }
  ]
}

### Delete the recipe -> 204 without a body (send twice: 404 the second time)
### Check afterwards: "Testzutat" is still in ingredient. The cascade runs from a
### recipe to its lines only, never on to the ingredient.
DELETE {{host}}/recipes/{{throwawayRecipe.response.body.$.id}}

### Unknown but valid UUID -> 404
DELETE {{host}}/recipes/00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000000

### Not a UUID -> 400
DELETE {{host}}/recipes/hallo


### ───────────── GET /ingredients ─────────────

### All ingredients, ordered by name, at most 20 -> 200
GET {{host}}/ingredients

### Case does not matter: finds Salz -> 200
### The search term passes through the same normalisation as the column.
GET {{host}}/ingredients?search=SALZ

### Spaces around the term: finds Salz -> 200
GET {{host}}/ingredients?search=%20salz%20

### Decomposed umlaut (O + diaeresis): finds Öl -> 200
### The case ILIKE alone does not solve — NFC normalisation does the work here.
GET {{host}}/ingredients?search=O%CC%88l

### Search term of spaces only: no filter, same list as without search -> 200
GET {{host}}/ingredients?search=%20%20

### Search without a hit -> 200 with []
GET {{host}}/ingredients?search=xyz


### ───────────── POST /ingredients ─────────────

### Create an ingredient -> 201 (409 when sent a second time)
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Liebstöckel", "defaultUnit": "PIECE" }

### An existing ingredient spelled differently -> 409
### The unique index sits on name_normalized, not on name. "Salz" from the seed
### and "  SALZ  " are the same row.
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "  SALZ  " }

### Ingredient without defaultUnit -> 201 (the field is optional)
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Lorbeerblatt" }

### Name of spaces only -> 400 (trimmed before it is validated)
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "   " }

### Unknown field id -> 400 (the database assigns the id)
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Kurkuma", "id": "abc" }

### Unit outside the enum -> 400
POST {{host}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Petersilie", "defaultUnit": "EL" }
